jobs.description:
As an Electrical Panel Technician, you will be responsible for assembling, wiring, and testing electrical control cabinets and operating panels. You will work from electrical schematics and technical drawings to ensure all systems are built according to the required specifications and quality standards.

Your main responsibilities include:

- Reading and interpreting electrical drawings and diagrams;
- Mounting electrical components and hardware;
- Wiring and assembling control cabinets and panels;
- Testing and inspecting completed systems before delivery;
- Supporting installation or commissioning work when needed.
- Most of your activities will take place in the workshop, with occasional on-site assignments at customer locations.

- MBO-level education in Electrical Engineering or similar;
- Experience with panel building or electrical assembly work is preferred;
- Ability to read and understand electrical schematics;
- Accurate and independent working attitude;
- Team player with a hands-on mentality;
- Good command of English (Dutch is an advantage).

As an Industrial Service Electrician, you will perform installation, maintenance, and repair work on industrial electrical systems. You will work on projects involving machinery, control cabinets, cable systems, and power installations. Safety and quality are essential in your daily work.

Your responsibilities include:

- Installing industrial cabling and electrical components;
- Maintaining and testing electrical systems;
- Analyzing and solving technical faults;
- Reading and interpreting technical drawings;
- Supporting project teams during installation activities.

- MBO-level education in Electrical Engineering or similar;
- Experience with industrial electrical installations;
- VCA certification is preferred;
- Knowledge of industrial safety standards is an advantage;
- Flexible and hands-on mentality;
- Good command of Dutch or English.

As an Electrical & Instrumentation Technician, you will be responsible for installing, maintaining, and troubleshooting electrical and instrumentation systems within industrial environments. You will work with control systems, sensors, measuring equipment, electrical panels, and automated installations that are essential for reliable production processes.

Your daily activities include:

- Installing, maintaining, and repairing electrical and instrumentation systems;
- Calibrating, testing, and commissioning instrumentation equipment;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical and technical faults;
- Performing inspections and preventive maintenance activities;
- Ensuring compliance with safety regulations, including ATEX requirements;
- Supporting production and engineering teams with technical expertise.

Depending on the project, you may work at industrial production sites, processing plants, or workshop facilities.

- Completed MBO level 3 or 4 education in Electrical Engineering, Instrumentation, or a related technical discipline;
- Relevant experience within industrial electrical engineering or E&I environments;
- Knowledge of NEN standards and ATEX regulations is preferred;
- VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driver’s license B;
- Strong analytical and problem-solving skills;
- Good command of the Dutch and/or English language

Are you detail-oriented, quality-focused, and looking for a full-time job in a dynamic logistics environment? Then this opportunity as a Quality Control Employee in Lelystad could be the perfect fit for you!

As a Quality Control Employee, you play a key role in ensuring that products meet the highest quality standards before moving further through the logistics process. You will work in a supportive team environment and be part of a 2-shift schedule (morning and afternoon shifts)

As a Quality Control Employee, your responsibilities include:

- Inspecting products to ensure they meet quality standards;
- Identifying, reporting, and helping resolve product defects;
- Carefully checking products for damages, errors, or irregularities;
- Maintaining a clean and organized work area;
- Contributing to an efficient and high-quality logistics operation;
- Following quality and safety procedures at all times.

- Basic English communication skills are required;
- Full-time availability;
- Strong attention to detail and quality;
- Ability to work effectively in a team environment;
- Ability to follow instructions accurately;
- Previous experience in quality control, production, or logistics is an advantage, but not required.

As a Shipboard Electrician, you will be responsible for installing, maintaining, and troubleshooting electrical systems onboard ships and maritime installations. You will work with a variety of systems, including power distribution, lighting, navigation equipment, automation systems, and communication networks.

Your daily responsibilities include:

- Installing and connecting electrical systems onboard vessels;
- Reading and interpreting technical drawings and electrical schematics;
- Inspecting, testing, and commissioning maritime electrical installations;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical and technical faults;
- Performing maintenance and repair activities on onboard systems;
- Supporting refit, modernization, and new-build projects.

You will primarily work at shipyards, ports, and onboard vessels, with occasional travel required for project support and sea trials.

- Completed MBO education in Electrical Engineering, Mechatronics, or a related technical field;
- Relevant experience as an electrician, preferably within shipbuilding, maritime, or offshore environments;
- Knowledge of maritime electrical systems and regulations is an advantage;
- Valid VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B;
- Flexible, proactive, and solution-oriented attitude;
- Ability to work independently and as part of a team;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English.

As an E&I Maintenance Technician, you will be responsible for maintaining, installing, and troubleshooting electrical and instrumentation systems within industrial plants. You will work with control systems, sensors, measuring equipment, and electrical installations to keep industrial processes running smoothly.

Your responsibilities include:

- Installing and connecting instrumentation and electrical systems;
- Testing, calibrating, and commissioning measuring instruments;
- Performing preventive and corrective maintenance activities;
- Troubleshooting faults in electrical and control systems;
- Ensuring all work complies with safety standards and regulations, including ATEX guidelines.
- You will work independently as well as together with colleagues on industrial projects and maintenance operations.

- MBO level 3 or 4 in Electrical Engineering, Instrumentation, Mechatronics, or similar;
- Experience with E&I systems in industrial environments;
- Knowledge of NEN 3140 and preferably ATEX;
- Valid VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B;
- Accurate, proactive, and solution-oriented mindset;
- Good communication skills in Dutch or English.
